    "result_text": "All tests pass. The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest` (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract), and the full `mvn test` run is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event for owner creation, alongside the existing human-readable audit line.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New immutable event \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (`rest/controller/v1/`): a Java `record` (inherently immutable) with fields `seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event`. It serializes itself to compact JSON via a static Jackson 3 `JsonMapper` (`toJson()`), and `event` is fixed to the `OWNER_CREATED` constant through the `of(...)` factory.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n   - Added a static `AtomicLong AUDIT_EVENT_SEQUENCE` so `seq` is monotonically increasing across *every* create, independent of controller instance \u2014 giving the event stream a total order.\n   - After the existing `AUDIT.info(...)` line in `addOwner`, it now builds and logs the event:\n     ```java\n     OwnerCreatedEvent event = OwnerCreatedEvent.of(AUDIT_EVENT_SEQUENCE.incrementAndGet(),\n         owner.getId(), primaryIdentifier(owner), ownerDto.getMembershipLevel());\n     AUDIT.info(event.toJson());\n     ```\n   - Added a `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. This is the **single point** that decides the owner's primary identifier \u2014 satisfying the spec's forward-looking requirement: when the customerCode is later unified into a memberId, redirecting this one method makes the event carry the memberId instead, with no other change.\n\nExample emitted line:\n```\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier`) confirms an AUDIT event line carries the `OWNER_CREATED` marker, the owner id, and the owner's `customerCode`.",
